{"schema":1,"fm":{"schema":1,"id":"merch-drop-track","kind":"workflow","title":"Merch drop track","description":"Takes a creator's merch from idea to shipped - testing demand, choosing print-on-demand or bulk stock, pricing from real unit costs, running a time-limited drop, then fulfilment and a post-mortem.","category":"creator-business","version":"1.0.0","status":"incubating","stage":["discover","plan","build","ship","review"],"role":["content-creator","founder"],"requires":["none"],"inputs":["notes","preferences","dataset"],"output":["plan","table","checklist","report"],"risk":"read-only","advice_risk":["financial","legal"],"invocation":"user","effort":"deep","interaction":"interactive","model_tier":"frontier","reasoning":"recommended","level":"intermediate","depth":"specific","tags":["merch","print-on-demand","preorders","unit-economics","product-drop"],"pairs_with":{"prompts":["design-merch-concepts","plan-creator-monetization"],"personas":["creator-business-manager"]},"args":[{"name":"idea","description":"What merch you are thinking of, the in-jokes or designs your audience asks for, and why now.","type":"text","required":true},{"name":"audience","description":"Audience size and engagement per platform, email list size, where your audience lives (countries), and any past sales (products, units, prices).","type":"text","required":true},{"name":"constraints","description":"Optional. Budget you can risk on stock, storage space, time you can give, and your country.","type":"text"}],"steps":[{"id":"demand","file":"steps/01-test-demand.md","stage":"discover","gate":"approve","artifact":"merch/01-demand.md"},{"id":"model","file":"steps/02-choose-the-model.md","stage":"plan","gate":"approve","artifact":"merch/02-model.md"},{"id":"price","file":"steps/03-price-the-range.md","stage":"plan","gate":"approve","artifact":"merch/03-pricing.md"},{"id":"drop","file":"steps/04-run-the-drop.md","stage":"build","gate":"approve","artifact":"merch/04-drop-plan.md"},{"id":"close","file":"steps/05-fulfil-and-review.md","stage":"review","gate":"none","artifact":"merch/05-post-mortem.md"}],"authorship":"ai-assisted","authors":["gabrielanhaia"],"last_reviewed":"2026-10-11","changelog":[{"version":"1.0.0","note":"First version."}]},"body":"Runs a merch drop the way a careful creator business would: prove people will buy before spending on stock, pick the production model that fits the risk, price from real landed costs, sell in a time-limited window, then deliver what was promised and learn from the numbers. Each step writes one artifact and waits for approval.\n\n<idea>\n{{idea}}\n</idea>\n\n<audience>\n{{audience}}\n</audience>\n\n{{#constraints}}\n<constraints>\n{{constraints}}\n</constraints>\n{{/constraints}}\n\nRules for every step:\n- You give general information, not professional advice. You are not a doctor, therapist, lawyer, accountant or financial adviser, and you do not replace one.\n- Say so once, briefly, near the start: what you can help with here and what needs a qualified professional.\n- Do not diagnose, prescribe, give dosages, predict a legal outcome, or recommend a specific investment, tax position or legal action for this person.\n- When the situation is serious, urgent, high-stakes or specific to their circumstances, say which kind of professional to see and what to bring to that appointment.\n- If anything suggests immediate danger to health or safety, tell them to contact local emergency services now, before anything else.\n- Rules, prices and laws differ by country and change over time. Name the assumption you are making and tell them to check it locally.\n- Use only figures the user gives or gets from suppliers. Never invent supplier prices, platform fees, shipping rates or conversion rates; where a number is needed, show the formula and mark the input [X] or as a stated assumption.\n- Designs must be the creator's own or properly licensed: no game logos, film characters, brand marks or fan art without permission.\n- Consumer rules (returns, delivery promises, product safety and labelling, especially for children's items) and sales tax or VAT differ by country. Flag them as checks with an accountant or local guidance, not conclusions.\n- Promise delivery times only from the supplier's stated times plus a buffer.\n- End each artifact with open questions.","steps":[{"id":"demand","file":"steps/01-test-demand.md","stage":"discover","gate":"approve","artifact":"merch/01-demand.md","text":"# Step 1: Test demand\n\n1. Who would buy: the share of the audience that is engaged enough to pay, where they live (shipping cost and time), and the in-jokes or symbols that mean something to them.\n2. Cheap tests before spending: a poll with mock-ups, a waitlist or interest form with an email field, a small preorder, or a single item on print-on-demand. Pick one or two and say what result would justify going ahead (for example sign-ups as a share of engaged viewers), stated as the creator's own threshold, not a market benchmark.\n3. A short post or script to run the test.\n4. Decision: go, adjust (different item or design), or stop.\n\nSections: Likely buyers, Tests, Test post, Decision rule, Open questions.\n\nStop and wait for approval."},{"id":"model","file":"steps/02-choose-the-model.md","stage":"plan","gate":"approve","artifact":"merch/02-model.md","text":"# Step 2: Choose the production model\n\n1. Compare print-on-demand (no stock risk, lower margin, less control over quality), bulk stock from a manufacturer (better margin and quality, cash and storage risk, unsold stock), preorder-then-produce (no stock risk, long wait for buyers), and a merch partner or agency (less work, smaller share).\n2. For this creator: the recommended model, given demand evidence, budget at risk, storage and time.\n3. Supplier checklist: sample before ordering, print quality and sizes, production and shipping times, minimum order quantities, returns and misprint policy, where they ship from and duties to buyers' countries.\n4. A short message to request quotes and samples.\n\nSections: Models compared, Recommendation, Supplier checklist, Quote request, Open questions.\n\nStop and wait for approval."},{"id":"price","file":"steps/03-price-the-range.md","stage":"plan","gate":"approve","artifact":"merch/03-pricing.md","text":"# Step 3: Price the range\n\n1. Landed unit cost per item: product, printing, packaging, platform and payment fees, shipping the creator pays, and an allowance for misprints and returns. Use supplier quotes; mark missing inputs [X].\n2. Price per item with margin per unit, and break-even units for any upfront spend.\n3. Range size: few items and sizes for a first drop; why.\n4. Shipping charges to buyers by region, and whether to absorb part.\n5. Check the price against what the audience can afford and what they have bought before; a sell-out at a fair price beats leftover stock.\n6. Checks for sales tax or VAT and import duties with an accountant or official guidance.\n\nSections: Unit costs, Prices and margins, Break-even, Range, Shipping charges, Tax checks, Open questions.\n\nStop and wait for approval."},{"id":"drop","file":"steps/04-run-the-drop.md","stage":"build","gate":"approve","artifact":"merch/04-drop-plan.md","text":"# Step 4: Run the drop\n\n1. Drop window and why time-limited (concentrated demand, known order quantities), with honest deadlines only.\n2. Announcement plan across platforms: tease, open, mid-drop reminder, last day, closed. Content ideas that show the item on the creator, not only mock-ups.\n3. Store page copy: item details, sizing guide, materials, care, production and delivery times stated from the supplier's times plus buffer, returns policy.\n4. Sponsorship-style conflicts: any current sponsor deal that restricts selling similar products.\n5. Customer service plan: where questions go, template replies for sizing, delays and wrong items.\n\nSections: Drop window, Announcement plan, Store page copy, Conflicts to check, Customer service, Open questions.\n\nStop and wait for approval."},{"id":"close","file":"steps/05-fulfil-and-review.md","stage":"review","gate":"none","artifact":"merch/05-post-mortem.md","text":"# Step 5: Fulfil and review\n\n1. Fulfilment checklist: orders to supplier, quality check of first units, shipping updates, and a delay message ready to send if needed.\n2. Results from the user's actual numbers: units by item and size, revenue, costs, margin, refunds, and time spent.\n3. What sold, what did not, and why that is likely; sizes or items to drop.\n4. Next drop: keep, change or stop merch, with the reason.\n\nSections: Fulfilment checklist, Results, What sold, Next drop, Open questions."}]}
